Structured Audition Form:
  Goal: replace the freeform audition editor with a structured form. Every audition still ends up as freeform HTML (old auditions keep theirs untouched); the form becomes the input that generates it.
  "Build without AI" = Blade template; "Build with AI" = Google Gemini restyles that same page from the poster.

  ✔ REMINDER: set up a Google Gemini API account (key → .env, never committed) and wire it into Phase 5 @done(26-11-16 14:27)
    - GEMINI_API_KEY is in local .env; add it to the production .env too (then `php artisan config:clear` if config is cached)
    - optional .env overrides: GEMINI_MODEL (default gemini-3.8-flash), GEMINI_FALLBACK_MODEL (default gemini-3.5-flash), GEMINI_TIMEOUT (default 150s)
  ☐ Keep testing "Build with AI" until gemini-3.8-flash itself answers (so far its 503s fell back to gemini-3.5-flash, which worked)

Phase 1 – Schema:
  ✔ 1.1 Migration 2026_11_16_000000: add to auditions @done(26-11-16 14:27)
    - what_to_expect, location (null = ACT's address), registration_url (blank for now), registration_note (null = default note), script_url
    - rehearsal_start (dateTime) + rehearsal_schedule (free text)
    - contacts (json): ordered [{name, title, phone, email}]; null = the show's director (replaces the planned contacts_overridden flag)
  ✔ 1.2 audition_sessions: end_time, note, is_callback; `session` datetime stays as the start @done(26-11-16 14:27)
  ✔ 1.3 audition_roles: gender_age, sort_order; notes (= description) now nullable @done(26-11-16 14:27)
  ✔ 1.4 config/act.php: ACT's address + default registration note @done(26-11-16 14:27)
  ✔ 1.5 Models: fillable/casts; Audition sessions(), callbacks(), roles() @done(26-11-16 14:27)

